# Maintain Cursor rules

When you **add, remove, or materially change** architecture, surfaces, or invariants, update project guidance in the **same task**.

## Checklist

1. Matching numbered rule under `.cursor/rules/` (table in `.cursor/README.md`)
2. `AGENTS.md` — one-line bullet if agent-relevant
3. `.cursor/README.md` — only if you add a **new** `.mdc` file
4. `docs/design-spec.md` — only for product-contract changes

## When to add a new `.mdc`

- New **domain** with its own globs (e.g. a second app surface)
- Otherwise **extend** an existing decade (`45_`, `55_`, …); avoid duplicates

## Style

- Actionable and short; paths + invariants over prose
- Link to `docs/design-spec.md` for deep specs
- Never document secrets

Skipping rule updates is only OK for typo/comment-only changes with no behavioural impact.
